{"key":"i07-s0003","rationale":"Idea:\nThe evolution from Version 1 to Version 2 demonstrated the significant benefits of a more explicit and consistent spike-driven architecture, particularly within the MLP block. Version 2 replaced the analog GELU + spike-gating mechanism with a direct intermediate spiking neuron, and critically, applied dropout directly to binary spikes before feeding them to the subsequent linear layer. This approach enforced a more ","callouts":{"1":"Spike encoder after each pre-norm: a standalone LIF layer converts the normalised stream into binary spikes, so every sub-layer receives a spike train; the projections' own neurons then re-spike an already binary input.","2":"Intermediate spiking neuron: fc1's analog output drives a LIF layer instead of GELU, and fc2 receives its (dropped-out) binary spikes."},"notes":[{"text":"dropout on spikes","kind":"evolved"}],"meta":"Iteration 7 · sample 3  ·  LightNet state update","nodes":{"n1":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L275","tip":null},"e1":{"label":"LIF","code":"L278-L280","tip":null,"novel":1},"q":{"label":"q proj","code":"L169","tip":null},"k":{"label":"k proj","code":"L170","tip":null},"v":{"label":"v proj","code":"L171","tip":null},"gp":{"label":"g proj","code":"L172","tip":null},"ws":{"label":"logσ","code":"L193","tip":null},"core":{"label":"LightNet","code":"L46-L157","tip":null},"onorm":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L209","tip":null},"oproj":{"label":"o proj","code":"L210","tip":null},"a1":{"label":"+","code":"L289","tip":null},"n2":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L293","tip":null},"e2":{"label":"LIF","code":"L296-L298","tip":null,"novel":1},"fc1":{"label":"fc1","code":"L232","tip":null},"lif":{"label":"LIF","code":"L235-L237","tip":null,"novel":2},"fc2":{"label":"fc2","code":"L245","tip":null},"a2":{"label":"+","code":"L306","tip":null},"core/dec":{"label":"exp","code":"L58,L65,L72","tip":null},"core/dm":{"label":"⊙","code":"L78","tip":null},"core/kv":{"label":"⊙","code":"L48","tip":null},"core/upd":{"l